re ready for this the end of  2021  so we are talking like a long time  now the idea here though is that if we  can control the path of the virus the  economy may do better  jerome powell the federal reserve  chairman has basically said hey  look at the path of the virus that will  tell you where the economy is going next  jill a lot of workers right now are  caught in this vicious cycle of being  laid off and then rehired and laid off  and then rehired the end of the paycheck  protection program  it seems like that means a final layoff  is coming for some of them it may be  good for businesses but it's not good  for workers  so how do you fix that well there has to  be some fix  if you want to do if you want to help  the small business universe  we have a survey out from cornell  university  which found some staggering numbers  found that  31 of those surveyed were actually  rehired by the payroll protection  program  then were laid off again and then we'd  say  another 26 percent say they too think  they will be laid off in the future  it is grim for small business they  probably need help more than  anyone any other type of business as  well as their  employees who need that six hundred  dollars a week  okay jules lessinger as always thank you  very much
 

